édélec elements in a cylindrical cell (radius and half-height 1.2 µm) inside a 1 µm PML, radial in ρ and Cartesian in z, which the fibre runs through; mirror symmetry halves it twice, so each orientation is a quarter problem (~100k unknowns, the middle mesh: 0.25 µm in vacuum, 0.06 µm in the fibre). The rate is Im(p·E) at the dipole over the same on the same mesh with the fibre's permittivity set to 1. TE₀₁ and TM₀₁ are cut off at 0.678 µm; just above it their fields reach far into the vacuum. The difference shrinks with the mesh: worst 1.4% → 0.8% → 0.5% at 0.8 µm and 4.4% → 1.3% → 0.8% at 0.645 µm (FEM_NGSOLVE.md). An earlier spherical cell with a radial PML met the guided modes badly and was off by up to 8–11% here; Meep agrees to 0.74% over the same band.","script":"benchmarks/figures.py","function":"ngsolve_cylinder_fibre"}
